1. PLACEMENT — item 1
=========================================================================

Every slot sits at the control that failed and is visible without scrolling
on a laptop, once the admin has done what triggers it:

  Reports modal, both errors showing (upload + save), panel 608px:
    1366x657  panel y 24..633   both fully visible, Save on screen
    1280x632  panel y 12..620   both fully visible, Save on screen
    1024x768 / 768x1024 / 360x740 (654px): same
  Careers modal (scrolls; admin scrolled to Save and clicked it): the error
    above Save is fully visible at every size; Save stays partly in view and
    clickable (45 of 48px on laptops, 23 of 48px at 360px) because the new
    line pushes it down. Placing it below Save would put it off-screen.
  Table delete rows: directly under the row. Leader cards: bottom of the
    card, next to Remove, shared by that card's save and delete. Add Leader:
    directly under the button.

Screen readers: each slot is <p role="alert">, conditionally mounted, so it
is announced on insertion and on any change of text. With no error, no
role="alert" node exists (checked in every idle state; e.g. after a
successful upload the alert list is []). No empty live region anywhere.

Found and fixed:
  a) TABLES CLIPPED THE DELETE BUTTON AND ITS ERROR (pre-existing clipping,
     new consequence). The tables need 682px (Reports) / 687px (Careers).
     The card was overflow-hidden:
       360px  card shows 294px  -> Year, Status, Actions cut off
       768px  card shows 414px  -> Status, Actions cut off
       1024px card shows 670px  -> 12/17px of padding cut, Delete visible
     overflow:hidden gives no scrollbar and ignores wheel/touch, so below
     ~1030px a mouse or touch user could not reach Delete at all (only Tab
     focus scrolled it into view), and the new delete error was laid out at
     the table's full width and cut mid-sentence (lines to x=512 against a
     visible edge at 327 on a phone; see 01, 02).
     Fix: the card scrolls (overflow-x-auto) and is a size container; the
     error is `sticky left-6` with max-width calc(100cqw - 3rem), i.e. pinned
     to the card's visible left edge and wrapped to its VISIBLE width.
     Measured AFTER, error lines vs visible box:
       360px  unscrolled 57..312 in 33..327 | scrolled 388px to Delete: same
       768px  unscrolled 329..687 in 305..719 | scrolled 268px: same
     Every Delete button is reachable by scrolling at every width (10-14).
     The card's scrollbar is 8px (matching globals.css's page scrollbar,
     which only sets width) so the 12px scroll left at 1024px is not a 16px
     default bar (13). Fallback if container queries are unsupported: the
     max-width declaration is dropped and the error renders as before.
  b) Row and error read as one unit: the failed row loses its bottom divider
     while its error shows; the error row's top padding went with it.
  c) REPORTS MODAL COULD NOT SCROLL. It never had a scroll path; T-015's two
     slots make it up to ~90px taller. 1280x560 BEFORE: panel y -24..584, the
     title and X above the viewport with no way to reach them (05). Fix:
     backdrop overflow-y-auto + panel my-auto (auto margins, so the top is
     never pushed out of reach). AFTER: panel 0..608, backdrop scrolls to
     Save (23). At every size where it fits, positions are identical to
     BEFORE (1366x657 24..633, 1280x632 12..620): nothing moves.
  d) LEADER REMOVE BUTTON OUTSIDE ITS CARD at 360px: the Photo URL input's
     default ~200px width (size=20) overflowed a 180px row; the input spilled
     past the card's padding and Remove sat at x 306..338, outside the card
     (65..295) (03). Fix: min-w-0 on the field's wrapper. AFTER: input
     90..222, Remove 238..270, inside the card (40). 768/1024/1366 unchanged.

=========================================================================
2. WORDING — item 2
=========================================================================

Server-returned text is untouched and shown verbatim ("Your session expired.
Sign in again and retry.", "Report not found. Reload the page to see the
current list.", etc.). Only the client fallbacks for a THROW changed:

  saves (Reports, Careers, leader blur-save)  T-012's text, unchanged:
    "Something went wrong saving these changes. Check your connection and
     try again."  (same wording as the six settings pages)
  Reports delete   "Couldn't delete this report. Check your connection and
                    try again."
  Careers delete   "Couldn't delete this job posting. Check your connection
                    and try again."
  Add Leader       "Couldn't add a leader. Check your connection and try
                    again."
  Leader remove    "Couldn't remove this leader. Check your connection and
                    try again."   ("remove" matches the button and confirm())
  Report upload    "Couldn't upload this PDF. Files must be under 1 MB. If
                    this one is, check your connection and try again."

The upload fallback names the limit because a real report PDF over Next's
default 1 MB Server Action body limit is rejected before uploadFile runs and
arrives here as a throw (SEC-INFO-35). That is the likeliest failure for a
real annual report, and "check your connection" alone would send the admin
retrying a file that can never upload. A code comment ties the line to
next.config.ts (no serverActions.bodySizeLimit set) so a future limit change
updates it. Admin UI microcopy, not marketing copy: no /copywriter or /cmo
review applies.

