3. IN-FLIGHT STATE AND KEYBOARD — item 3
=========================================================================

Busy state on the triggering control:
  Modal Save            spinner + "Saving..."  (already there)
  Upload, empty state   spinner + "Uploading...", disabled (already there)
  Upload, Replace       NOTHING BEFORE: label stayed "Replace" while X and
                        Save went disabled with no explanation (04, /cso's
                        /ui-ux nit). FIXED: spinner + "Uploading..." (31).
                        Deliberately NOT disabled: disabling a focused button
                        drops focus to <body> with nothing to restore it, and
                        /cso traced that a second pick queues in order.
  Add Leader            WAS disabled but looked identical (opacity 1, hover
                        tint still applied). FIXED: disabled:opacity-50, hover
                        tint only when enabled (43). No spinner on purpose:
                        isPending is shared with leader blur-saves and the
                        page's Save Changes, so it cannot say what is running.
  Modal X (disabled)    brightened to white on hover while disabled. FIXED:
                        enabled:hover:text-white (stays white/40 when disabled).
  New spinners use motion-safe:animate-spin; the existing ones in these
  files were switched too (the compiled rule sits inside
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference)).

Keyboard, measured on the real component (unchanged by this pass):
  Tab order in the Reports modal: X first in DOM order; measured from Title:
    Category, Year, Upload/Replace, Published, Save; Tab after Save leaves
    the document.
  Enter on Save: Save turns disabled, and Chrome's focus fix-up moves focus
    to <body> for the rest of the request and after it.
  Escape while a save or upload is in flight: modal stays open. Backdrop
    click during an upload: stays open. (The modal has no Escape handler in
    any state, so nothing bypasses T-015's no-dismiss rule.)
  After the failure: focus is on <body>. Pressed from that state, Shift+Tab
    lands on "Published" (then the upload button), back inside the modal;
    Tab leaves the page. Focus is not trapped, but it is not returned
    either (follow-up F1).
  Identical retry (same failure twice): the SAME <p role="alert"> node
    persists with identical text, so it is not re-announced (follow-up F2).

Focus rings: no outline is removed on any touched button. Delete/Edit get
Chrome's default :focus-visible ring (outline auto, #005fcc with a white
edge, 3.2:1 on #0f0f0f), reached by real Tab presses (14-15 Tabs; 50).
Accessible names: lucide 0.575 marks every icon aria-hidden, so the icon-only
Edit, Delete, Close and Remove buttons were announced as just "button".
FIXED with aria-labels: "Edit <title>", "Delete <title>", "Close",
"Remove <name>" (fallback nouns for an empty title/name, as in
CategoryProductsManager). Measured names, e.g. "Delete Sustainability Report
2024", "Remove Sharifur Rahman Jr." (follows the typed name).

