=========================================================================
7. NOT CHANGED HERE — behavior-level follow-ups (for /pm; each changes
   handler logic in src/app/admin/**, so each needs /cso)
=========================================================================

F1 Focus after a failed save or add: native `disabled` on the pressed button
   drops focus to <body>. Return it to the button (or the alert) after a
   failure. Best done inside F3.
F2 An identical repeated failure is not re-announced: setError(null) runs
   inside the async transition, so React defers it to the end of the
   action; the alert node never unmounts. Same shape in T-012's six
   settings clients. Fix pattern: clear the error BEFORE startTransition.
   Apply to all nine surfaces at once.
F3 Neither modal has dialog semantics (role="dialog", aria-modal,
   aria-labelledby), initial focus, focus containment (Tab walks into the
   page behind) or Escape-to-close. The native <dialog> + showModal() gives
   containment, an inert background and Escape with no new library; block
   its `cancel` event while a request is in flight to keep T-015's
   no-dismiss rule; restore focus to the opener on close.
F4 A client-side file.size check before uploadFile would show the 1 MB
   message instantly. Fits SEC-INFO-33's recommended small ticket.
F5 isPending is shared on Who We Are: a leader blur-save or Add Leader
   shows "Saving..." on the page's Save Changes and disables it, and the
   page Save disables Add Leader. Separate transitions per action. Pre-existing.
F6 Row Delete buttons show no in-flight state (needs per-row pending state).

